{title: 408 - Lord, Enthroned in Heavenly Splendor}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #408 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 408}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Lord, [Em]enthroned [C]in [Am]heav'nly splendor,
[Em/B]First [Am]begotten [Em]from [C]the dead,
[Em]You [G7/F]alone, [Am/C]our [F#m]strong [G]defender,
[G]Lifting [F#m]up [G]Your [Em]people's [Am/E]head.
[Em]Alleluia, [G]Jesus, [Em]true [G7]and living [C]Bread!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Tho' [Em]the [Dm]lowliest [Am]form [G]now [Am]veil You
[Em/B]As [Am]of [G]old [Am]in [Em]Bethlehem,
[Em]Here [G7/F]as [Am]there Your [F#m]angels [Am]hail [Dm]You
[G]Branch and [F#m]flow'r [G]of [Em]Jesse's [Am/E]stem.
[Em]Alleluia, [G]We [Em]in worship [G7/D]join with [C]them.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Paschal [Dm]Lamb, [C]Your [Am]off'ring finished
[Em/B]Once [Am]for [G]all [Am]when [Em]You [C]were slain,
[Em]In [G7/F]its [Am]fullness [F#m]undiminished
[G]Shall forever [Em]more remain.
[Em]Alleluia, [G]Cleansing [Em]souls from [G7]every [C]stain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Life [Em]imparting [Am]heav'nly manna,
[Em/B]Stricken [G]rock [Am]with [Em]streaming [C]side,
[Em]Heav'n [G7/F]and [Am]earth with [F#m]loud [G]hosanna
[G]Worship [F#m]You [G]the [Em]Lamb who [Am/E]died.
[Em]Alleluia, Ris'n, ascended, [G7/D]glorified!
{end_of_verse}
